$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7S,13R,19R-Tris(tert-butyldimethylsilanyloxy)-9S-hydroxy-21S-(4-methoxy-benzyloxy)-6S,12S,14S,20R,22S-pentamethylhexacosa-2Z,4E,10Z,23Z-tetraenoate
(21a-α). A solution of vinyl iodide 3 (77 mg, 0.095 mmol, azeotropically
dried with toluene) in dry Et2O (1 mL) was treated with t-BuLi (0.122 mL,
0.208 mmol, 1.7 M in pentane) at -78 °C. After 30 min, a solution of
aldehyde 4a (62 mg, 0.190 mmol, azeotropically dried with toluene) in
Et2O (0.7 mL) was added dropwise via syringe. The reaction mixture was
stirred at -78 °C for 2 h, then quenched with saturated NH4Cl. The
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O, washed with brine, and dried over
MgSO4. After filtration and concentration, the crude product was purified
by flash chromatography (SiO2, 20:1 hexanes/EtOAc). The de-iodide side
product 22 (22 mg, 33.6%), less polar undesired β-alcohol 21a-β (18 mg,
18.7%) and the desired polar α-alcohol 21a-α (28 mg, 29.2%, containing
some impurities) as a colorless oil. 21a-α. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.40 (dd, J = 15.6, 11.4 Hz, 1H), 7.28 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 6.86 (d, J =
7.8Hz, 2H), 6.54 (t, J = 11.1 Hz, 1H), 6.15 (dd, J = 15.6, 6.6 Hz, 1H),
5.58 (d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1H), 5.51-5.44 (m, 2H), 5.36-5.29 (m, 2H), 4.61 (t,
J = 8.7 Hz, 1H), 4.55 (d, J = 10.2 Hz, 1H), 4.48 (d, J = 10.2 Hz, 1H),
3.91 (br s, 1H), 3.79 (s, 3H), 3.71 (s, 3H), 3.62 (br s, 1H), 3.35-3.34
