7S,13R,19R-Tris(tert-butyldimethylsilanyloxy)-9S-hydroxy-21S-(4-methoxy-benzyloxy)-6S,12S,14S,20R,22S-pentamethylhexacosa-2Z,4E,10Z,23Z-tetraenoate
(21a-α). A solution of vinyl iodide 3 (77 mg, 0.095 mmol, azeotropically
dried with toluene) in dry Et2O (1 mL) was treated with t-BuLi (0.122 mL,
0.208 mmol, 1.7 M in pentane) at -78 °C. After 30 min, a solution of
aldehyde 4a (62 mg, 0.190 mmol, azeotropically dried with toluene) in
Et2O (0.7 mL) was added dropwise via syringe. The reaction mixture was
stirred at -78 °C for 2 h, then quenched with saturated NH4Cl. The
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O, washed with brine, and dried over
MgSO4. After filtration and concentration, the crude product was purified
by flash chromatography (SiO2, 20:1 hexanes/EtOAc).
7S,13R,19R-Tris-(tert-butyldimethylsilanoxy)-9S-hydroxy-21S-(4-methoxy-benzyloxy)-6R,12S,14S,20R,22S-pentamethylhexacosa-2Z,4E,10Z,23Z-tetraenoic
acid methyl ester (21b-α). In a procedure similar to the synthesis of
21a-α, a solution of vinyl iodide 3 (81 mg, 0.099 mmol) in dry ether (1
mL) was treated with t-BuLi (0.218 mmol, 0.13 mL, 1.7 M in pentane) at
-78 °C. After stirring for 1 h a solution of aldehyde 4b (71.4 mg, 0.218
mmol) in dry ether (0.5 mL) was added dropwise via syringe. Stirring
continued for 2 h, followed by the same work-up as described above and
flash chromatography (SiO2, 40:1-6:1 hexanes/EtOAc) to afford the desired
isomer 21b-α (24.5 mg, 24%), undesired isomer 21b-β (12.5 mg, 12%) and
de-iodinated product 22 (22.4 mg). 21b-α. Rf = 0.53 (3:1 hexanes/EtOAc);
[α]25 D + 31.2 (c 0.275, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.37 (dd, J =
15.5, 11.5 Hz, 1H), 7.28 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 6.85 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H),
6.54 (t, J = 11.5 Hz, 1H), 6.01 (dd, J = 15.0, 7.5 Hz, 1H), 5.59 (d, J =
11.0 Hz, 1H), 5.45 (quint, J = 10.5 Hz, 2H), 5.36-5.30 (m, 2H), 4.62 (t,
J = 8.5 Hz, 1H), 4.54 (d, J = 10.5 Hz, 1H), 4.47 (d, J =11.0 Hz, 1H),
3.94-3.90 (m, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 3.63-3.60 (m, 1H), 3.36
(dd, J = 5.5, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 3.28 (dd, J = 7.5, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 2.80-2.77 (m,
1H), 2.70-2.64 (m, 1H), 2.63-2.59 (m, 1H), 2.19 (s, 1H), 2.11-2.04 (m,
1H), 2.03-1.96 (m, 1H), 1.65 (ddd, J = 7.0, 7.0, 3.5 Hz, 1H), 1.60-1.55
(m, 2H), 1.54-1.48 (m, 2H), 1.44-1.37 (m, 2H), 1.36-1.29 (m, 3H),
1.18-1.12 (m, 2H), 1.05 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 6H), 0.97 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H),
0.96 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.95 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 0.91 (s, 9H), 0.90
(s, 9H), 0.88(s, 9H), 0.82 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H), 0.12 (s, 3H), 0.06 (s,
3H), 0.06 (s, 3H), 0.05 (s, 3H), 0.02 (s, 3H), 0.01 (s, 3H) ppm; 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.8, 158.9, 147.2, 145.3, 135.6, 131.6, 131.3, 131.2,
131.0, 129.0, 126.8, 115.7, 113.6, 84.4, 79.9, 77.2, 74.8, 72.8, 64.7,
55.3, 51.1, 42.8, 40.6, 40.1, 37.6, 36.2, 35.3, 34.6, 34.0, 31.9, 29.7,
26.2, 26.0, 25.9, 20.9,19.9, 19.0, 18.4, 18.2, 18.0, 14.5, 14.5, 14.4,
9.3, -3.4, -3.7, -3.8, -4.5, -4.5, -4.5 ppm; HRMS (ESI) calcd for
C58H106O8Si3Na [M + Na]+ 1037.7088, found 1037.7123.
